 hold the most record highs of any decade (81). Sioux City's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on July 4, 1936.","t_chg":"Sioux City's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 132 complete years: Sioux City's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.04\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.04) that includes zero. Sioux City's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.31), about +3.1\u00b0F since 1890.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; April and October fell. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Sioux City has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Sioux City's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.33 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.57), about +4.4 inches since 1890. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 29.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2014 (41.36 in); the driest, 1976 (14.33 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 10 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}